    "title": "IA Secretary of State Paul Pate warns voters about potential scams - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Reilly Mahon Maren Ewertz ,\n1 hours ago IOWA ( KCAU ) — Just as absentee voting in Iowa begins, Iowa Secretary of State Paul Pate is warning voters about potential text scams.\nPate said that people are getting texts from numbers impersonating elected officials and candidates in the hopes of scamming Iowans.\nStory continues below\nAlthough we are unaware of reports around Siouxland, Pate said that it is happening around many Iowa counties.\nThe fake message asks recipients about their top priorities, and then asks them to reply with thoughts or “Text STOP to opt out.” Pate said that legitimate outreach from candidates and pollsters will not ask for sensitive information.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to SiouxlandProud | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
